# The repository is edited on Windows and built on Linux. Git stores LF
# either way, but a CRLF working copy can still reach the image through a
# bind mount or a local `docker build`, and `sh` treats the trailing \r as
# part of the command. Pin the files where that would break a deploy.

* text=auto eol=lf

Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf

*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.pdf           binary
*.faiss         binary
*.pkl           binary
